  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Dehydrosoyasaponin I and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with this complex. Dehydrosoyasaponin I is linked to ME-180, which is a target of Alstolucine B and 2,2,2-Trideuterio-1-(2-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)ethanone, both of which have been shown to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Similarly, Dehydrosoyasaponin I is also linked to Yardenone, which targets the same complex. These findings collectively indicate that Dehydrosoyasaponin I may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, possibly through a common pathway involving ME-180 or other related compounds. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
